        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-18T22:26:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We use the hypercall based access to translation structures only after Translation is enabled. During initialization phase(before enabling translation) the host can directly access the translation structures through root table pointer and it sets up the translation structures and calls iommu_enable hypercall. It write protects the table and then hosts sets this flag. From then on, host cannot directly access the translation structures and then goes through hypercall. This flag is to denote that iommu is paravirt enabled and only hypercall access is allowed.\n\nI shall add comments to make it clear.",
      "parentUuid": "8f96f23d_5da9c2b1",
      "revId": "bcc18e7562506fc1e9414c064167da4ccdd5deec",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a543979c_ea6b1678",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.h",
        "patchSetId": 34
      },
      "lineNbr": 778,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-18T22:45:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But what\u0027s the problem to access them through hypercalls from the beginning?\n\nAlso just wondering: so still not all such accesses are prevented by aosp/3786912 ?",
      "parentUuid": "a7db6a40_84633953",
      "revId": "bcc18e7562506fc1e9414c064167da4ccdd5deec",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fc0c9872_d03cc1ff",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.h",
        "patchSetId": 34
      },
      "lineNbr": 778,
      "author": {
        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-18T22:59:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The in-memory translation structures could be directly accessed by host during initialization(not yet write protected) and hence we access it directly. It could be accessed via hypercalls as well, but thought of saving some round trip as the pages could be directly accessed. aosp/3786912 only prevents the QI MMIO accesses. Each translation table update would be usually followed by one or two QI submits so we save about ~3 hypercalls for each translation structure update.\n\nAs you mentioned in the other cl, the hypercall reduction will be in the order of tens and probably less than 100 mostly, so not sure if its worth it. I shall try to implement the blanket hypercall approach and take some numbers this week and see how much we are saving.",
      "parentUuid": "a543979c_ea6b1678",
      "revId": "bcc18e7562506fc1e9414c064167da4ccdd5deec",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7ec888bb_063cadd4",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.h",
        "patchSetId": 34
      },
      "lineNbr": 778,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-18T23:15:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah got it, so it is specifically about accessing structures in memory.\n\nSo, yeah, if performance is the only reason while in fact there no real measured performance win (so there is no reason at all), IMHO it\u0027s better to keep the code simpler.",
      "parentUuid": "fc0c9872_d03cc1ff",
      "revId": "bcc18e7562506fc1e9414c064167da4ccdd5deec",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dcc9f744_849fdd40",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.h",
        "patchSetId": 34
      },
      "lineNbr": 778,
      "author": {
        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-19T14:11:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I did a quick prototype with hypercalls for in-memory structures and qi enabled for initialization(before translation enable: revert aosp/3786912). I timed the `intel_iommu_init()` from function start to finish and here are the results on felino(average of 5 runs):\n(1) Existing implementation(no hypercall during initialization): 13.134 us\n(2) Hypercall for in-memory structures: 13.490 us\n(3) (2) with qi enabled: 13.688 us\n\nSo there is only about ~200-300 us improvement in the boot time and is not really significant. I shall modify the implementation to have a separate hypercall for SRTP and then remove extra logic needed for handling translation structures before and after translation. As you mentioned, this would make it much simpler.",
      "parentUuid": "7ec888bb_063cadd4",
      "revId": "bcc18e7562506fc1e9414c064167da4ccdd5deec",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
